    "derivation": "Hand-authored per D21. Argument names and the connection shape came from the orders query page; every Order field below was individually confirmed present on the Order object page (151 fields there; this is a subset). Values are invented. No live capture (D3).",
    "caveats": [
      "WHICH SUBSET the system reads is not specified anywhere in this repo — the ticket says only 'orders query subset'. The subset below is this stub's design decision, chosen to mirror the webhook payload field-for-field so the two surfaces agree.",
      "checkoutToken and cartToken ARE real Order fields in this API version — nullable Strings, no deprecation. The orders query page does not list them (it shows only a sample selection set), so their absence from that page is not evidence of absence from the type.",
      "DiscountCodeApplication has SIX fields, including `index`, which is easy to miss. Its `value` is the PricingValue union (MoneyV2 | PricingPercentageValue) and needs an inline fragment in a real selection set.",
      "The stub does not honour the selection set — it returns this whole node shape whatever was asked for. The response is therefore a SUPERSET of a narrowed real response, never a differently-shaped one, and the parity test asserts exactly that relation."
    ]
  },
